msgstr ""

#: ui/config/output_group.py:249
msgid ""
"<p>The rate this output's device runs at; the main output's sound is "
"converted to it (a band-limited interpolator, with the clocks' drift). "
"The device's: its own format (WASAPI's shared mix format), the lowest "
"latency. Another rate: in exclusive mode the device runs at it; shared, "
"the system converts it (WASAPI (cpal)'s usual stream, more latency).</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/output_group.py:258
msgid ""
"<p>The audio kept ahead of this output's device, from the main output's "
"mix: the least it holds whatever the two devices' periods (it holds up to"
" one main device period more as they fall). Smaller is heard sooner; too "
"small drops out when the computer is busy. Its device's own latency comes"
" after it.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/output_group.py:265
msgid ""
"<p>This device's clock against the main output's: how much faster (+) or "
"slower (-) it runs, in parts per million. The output is resampled by it "
"(a band-limited interpolator), so it neither runs dry nor fills up, and "
"nothing is repeated or dropped. A few tens to a few hundred ppm is usual "
"between two devices.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/output_group.py:270
msgid "Mix the master in"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/output_group.py:272
msgid ""
"<p>The headphones carry the channels whose CUE is on (before their "
"faders) and, with this on, the master, mixed by the CUE / MASTER mix (a "
"controller's knob moves it). Off for a controller that mixes the master "
"into its headphones itself (the DDJ-400's CUE / MASTER knob, in analog): "
"the headphones output then carries the CUE alone, silent while no CUE is "
"on.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/output_group.py:280
msgid ""
"<p>The master's share in the headphones: 0 % the CUE alone, 100 % the "
"master alone. A controller's CUE / MASTER knob moves it as it is "
"turned.</p>"
msgstr ""

